# Code owners: GitHub asks them to review every pull request that touches a matching path. Without
# a branch ruleset that requires code-owner review this is a request, not a gate. The last matching
# line wins, so the paths below override the catch-all. Replace @your-github-handle with a user or
# an @org/team; setup created this file once, and it is yours now.

*                                @your-github-handle

# CI, and what decides what reaches production.
/.github/                        @your-github-handle
/.gitleaks.toml                  @your-github-handle
/Dockerfile                      @your-github-handle
/go.mod                          @your-github-handle
/go.sum                          @your-github-handle

# The agent's guardrails: what it may run and reach, the lock that turns the hooks on, and the
# checks and scripts that judge and unlock its work. A one-line edit here can switch a guard off.
/.claude/settings.json           @your-github-handle
/.claude/agent-config-kit.lock   @your-github-handle
/.claude/agent-config.json       @your-github-handle
/.mcp.json                       @your-github-handle
/.golangci.yml                   @your-github-handle
/.githooks/                      @your-github-handle
/scripts/check/                  @your-github-handle
/scripts/ops/                    @your-github-handle
/scripts/env/                    @your-github-handle
/.skillspector-baseline.yaml     @your-github-handle

# The contract, the error codes, startup and the database: a mistake here reaches every client.
/api/openapi.yaml                @your-github-handle
/internal/apperr/                @your-github-handle
/internal/config/                @your-github-handle
/cmd/                            @your-github-handle
/db/                             @your-github-handle
